    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Currently I'm using the built-in omnicomplete, with `<c-x><c-o>`, and [nvim-snippy](https://github.com/dcampos/nvim-snippy) to expand LSP snippets. I understand that mini.completion doesn't support snippet expansion, but is there a way to include LSP snippets in the completion results so I can expand them with nvim-snippy?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Currently I'm using the built-in omnicomplete, with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;c-x&gt;&lt;c-o&gt;</code>, and <a href=\"https://github.com/dcampos/nvim-snippy\">nvim-snippy</a> to expand LSP snippets. I understand that mini.completion doesn't support snippet expansion, but is there a way to include LSP snippets in the completion results so I can expand them with nvim-snippy?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Currently I'm using the built-in omnicomplete, with <c-x><c-o>, and nvim-snippy to expand LSP snippets. I understand that mini.completion doesn't support snippet expansion, but is there a way to include LSP snippets in the completion results so I can expand them with nvim-snippy?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2023-10-15T17:54:32Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, there is a way, but it is not pretty.\r\n\r\nSnippets are filtered out when processing LSP response before creating an actual list of completion entries. This part can be configured by `config.lsp_completion.process_items()`. But the thing is, there is no exported way which doesn't filter out snippets. But you can try something like this, which is a cherry-picked version of 'mini.completion' code:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal get_completion_word =\r\n  function(item) return (item.textEdit or {}).newText or item.insertText or item.label or '' end\r\n\r\nlocal process_items_with_snippets = function(items, base)\r\n  local res = vim.tbl_filter(function(item) return vim.startswith(get_completion_word(item), base) end, items)\r\n  table.sort(res, function(a, b) return (a.sortText or a.label) < (b.sortText or b.label) end)\r\n  return res\r\nend\r\n\r\nrequire('mini.completion').setup({ lsp_completion = { process_items = process_items_with_snippets } })\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, there is a way, but it is not pretty.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Snippets are filtered out when processing LSP response before creating an actual list of completion entries. This part can be configured by <code class=\"notranslate\">config.lsp_completion.process_items()</code>. But the thing is, there is no exported way which doesn't filter out snippets. But you can try something like this, which is a cherry-picked version of 'mini.completion' code:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local get_completion_word =\n  function(item) return (item.textEdit or {}).newText or item.insertText or item.label or '' end\n\nlocal process_items_with_snippets = function(items, base)\n  local res = vim.tbl_filter(function(item) return vim.startswith(get_completion_word(item), base) end, items)\n  table.sort(res, function(a, b) return (a.sortText or a.label) &lt; (b.sortText or b.label) end)\n  return res\nend\n\nrequire('mini.completion').setup({ lsp_completion = { process_items = process_items_with_snippets } })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">get_completion_word</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> (<span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">textEdit</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> {}).<span class=\"pl-e\">newText</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">insertText</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">label</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">process_items_with_snippets</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">base</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">res</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">tbl_filter</span>(<span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">startswith</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">get_completion_word</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>), <span class=\"pl-smi\">base</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">table.sort</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">res</span>, <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">a</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">b</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> (<span class=\"pl-smi\">a</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">sortText</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">a</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">label</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span> (<span class=\"pl-smi\">b</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">sortText</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">b</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">label</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">res</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.completion<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({ <span class=\"pl-smi\">lsp_completion</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">process_items</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">process_items_with_snippets</span> } })</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "Yes, there is a way, but it is not pretty.\nSnippets are filtered out when processing LSP response before creating an actual list of completion entries. This part can be configured by config.lsp_completion.process_items(). But the thing is, there is no exported way which doesn't filter out snippets. But you can try something like this, which is a cherry-picked version of 'mini.completion' code:\nlocal get_completion_word =\n  function(item) return (item.textEdit or {}).newText or item.insertText or item.label or '' end\n\nlocal process_items_with_snippets = function(items, base)\n  local res = vim.tbl_filter(function(item) return vim.startswith(get_completion_word(item), base) end, items)\n  table.sort(res, function(a, b) return (a.sortText or a.label) < (b.sortText or b.label) end)\n  return res\nend\n\nrequire('mini.completion').setup({ lsp_completion = { process_items = process_items_with_snippets } })",
